WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.710
Hello there, I'm Gav.

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.543
I'm Dan.

00:00:02.543 --> 00:00:03.550
We're The Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.280
Dan, one of my favorite treats
back when I lived in the UK

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.860
was a lovely pack of Maltesers.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.240
Yeah, never used to be able
to get them in America,

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.880
but they've recently launched in the U.S.,

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.250
so they're all over the gaff now.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.220
So we thought, being from England,

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.300
why not give them our
own Slow Mo Guys launch?

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.160
Yeah, at 800 feet per second
with this massive air cannon.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.163
Hello, America.

00:00:22.115 --> 00:00:23.220
I'm here!

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.840
And we're gonna film it
at ridiculous frame rates

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.540
on the Phantom V2511.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.840
Shall we start with a melon?

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.510
Lets, I've got one
right here oddly enough.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.350
Let's do it.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.310
All right, so how does
this device work then?

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:37.230
Kinda complicated, but we got
high pressure nitrogen here,

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.050
fed through a tube all the way into here,

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:40.750
which is like a regulator valve.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.350
Now this, when it makes a sound,

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:44.976
That's a good sound.

00:00:44.976 --> 00:00:47.340
That's filling up the
chamber with pressure, okay?

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.580
Up to 150 PSI, which is regulated by that.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.570
When it stops making noise,
that means it's full.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:53.403
All right.

00:00:53.403 --> 00:00:55.530
Okay, so now we got our gas in here,

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.920
and this is like our valve to release it,

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.670
so it's armed and then you press fire,

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:00.770
and that's what releases the gas.

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:01.603
Solenoid?

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.630
Uh, it's called, yes, solenoid valve.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:05.840
That's right, well done.
Yes!

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.470
Venturi here, increases the pressure

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:08.900
going into the chamber,

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.237
and this here is our chamber
where we load the Malteser in.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.070
Oh, okay.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.520
So that's where we're going,
and if it fits, it sits.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.657
So you put it in there,

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:17.733
screw it up.

00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:18.566
Yep.

00:01:18.566 --> 00:01:19.750
And then we've got our tube here,

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.140
gets fired along here with the pressure,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.680
and our object that's gonna be

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.070
imminently destroyed sits here.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.200
That's the goodbye zone.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.380
Yeah, this isn't going to be here for

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.213
when we're shooting stuff,

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:30.810
but this is a tester to
find out how far stuff goes.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.490
What's our highest Malteser so far?

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.810
Fluke one, 900 feet per second,

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:36.930
which is faster than a .45 caliber round

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.112
that comes out of the muzzle of a pistol.

00:01:39.112 --> 00:01:39.945
Phew.

00:01:39.945 --> 00:01:41.340
So, it's pretty intense.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.700
We might as well be using a firearm.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.340
Might as well just be
sitting there with a pistol.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.006
Yeah.

00:01:46.006 --> 00:01:49.000
And then we got a backboard
over there to catch the mess.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.083
Yes, absolutely.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.970
Malteser, as you can see.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.220
Ready to get loaded
in, just pops in there.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.080
Screw this up, that's our chamber.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.830
Cool, okay, so I'm gonna gas the tube.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:02.663
Arming.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.003
Three, two, one.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.590
Oh!

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.810
Goodness me!

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.560
I think we need to clean our glass.

00:02:14.034 --> 00:02:15.294
Oh, that's the air?

00:02:15.294 --> 00:02:16.127
Oh!

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.525
What's that, is that just

00:02:18.525 --> 00:02:20.496
all the air being released?

00:02:20.496 --> 00:02:22.745
It comes with a lot of air.

00:02:22.745 --> 00:02:23.578
Whoa!

00:02:23.578 --> 00:02:24.700
I need to adjust the exposure,

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.230
there's a lot of air and
spray that's so bright.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.063
Yeah.

00:02:28.063 --> 00:02:29.430
All right, I think we
should do that again.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.540
So we've seen what
happens with one Malteser,

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.987
but what happens if we do two Maltesers?

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.310
Got two here,

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:38.830
let's see if we can bung
both of them in there.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:41.760
One, two.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.062
Ready for gas.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.030
Good sound, innit?

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.210
So meaty.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.743
Three, two, one!

00:02:48.675 --> 00:02:49.508
Whoa!

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.930
Bloody hell, that was a different spray.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:53.763
You got hit over there?

00:02:53.763 --> 00:02:55.433
I got watermelon brains on me.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.200
Here's our unsuspecting
watermelon just chilling out.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.950
That was a really good escalation.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:02.783
Yeah.

00:03:03.754 --> 00:03:05.224
Oh, wait!

00:03:05.224 --> 00:03:07.436
One after the other!

00:03:09.497 --> 00:03:10.720
